  "caveats": [
    "The two A=1 atoms share a value at zeta_6 (both tr_M == u mod Phi_6) while the A=2 atom does not, so this is NOT a universal evaluation of tr_M at a 6th root of unity. Whether the A=1 agreement is forced or coincidental is OPEN; no mechanism is claimed here.",
    "Exactness is bounded by DATA, not method: evaluating at p needs 2p+1 Habiro coefficients. With 9/9/14 available this reaches p<=3 for the nucleons and p<=5 for the deuteron. Nothing here speaks to larger primes.",
    "A unit at one prime refutes the no-exception-set form (for-all p) but NOT the almost-every-prime form; one prime is not a positive density."
